            "review_title": "Review at Veggie Castle - Nha Hang Chay Vegan",
            "review_text": "Darth_Vaider\nUnited Kingdom375 contributions\n0\nVery disappointing food.\nMay 2025 • Couples\nAfter eating really decent vegan food while in Hanoi, we were exited to try a vegan buffet.\n\nWe checked the reviews and most seemed to be ok, so we thought we would try this place for ourselves.\n\nSo let me start by saying we have been eating vegan food for almost a decade, so we know how things should and should not taste.\n\nWhen we arrived the first thing that surprised me was they wanted payment before we even sat down. They also weren’t very friendly about this either.\n\nSo I went up for my first plate and was shocked by the amount of flies on the food. So there were a few things I didn’t even go near. \n\nOnce I filled my plate I sat down and started eating. How disappointing!!! Everything apart from the rice was cold or tepid. Most dishes were just sat out on cold plates and those in hot plates weren’t even warm.\n\nI waited for my partner to come back and try their food before expressing what I thought. Just like me, they found the food to be cold and most things tasted nasty and were inedible. \n\nWe both agreed that these dishes must have been sitting out for multiple hours, because they were just awful and covered in flies. Fried tofu is one of my favourite things, yet their fried tofu was cold, had a strange texture and just tasted off. How can you make tofu taste this bad?! \n\nThe place also got very busy and we were glad to just leave.\n\nIt’s also interesting to see the price increases in such a short time, it is now 99,000 per person. Yet this clearly has not improved food quality. You will get much better food at a fraction of this cost in Hanoi, so try any other of the many vegan places to eat. \n\nI would not recommend this place, despite how the pictures look (although you’ll notice from the pictures how most of the food is uncovered and on cold plates). \n\nNow I realise why they make you pay first, because once you taste the food, you will not want to pay.\nRead more\nWritten May 5, 2025",
